hey this is presto Walker reminding you  to mind your decisions here's a fun  problem I found online  this unusual shape has three right  angles as marked also its side lengths  are four three four and five the  question is what is the value of the  last sides length which is marked as X  in the diagram pause if you'd like to  give it a try and when you're ready keep  watching to learn how to solve this  problem  [Music]  so briefly mention the solution I'm  going to present is very similar to  another video where you had to solve for  X the length of this square side we're  going to use a little outside the box  thinking so in our diagram the first  thing I'm going to do is I'm going to  draw it a little bit to scale this will  just help in our presentation now let's  connect these two points we're going to  figure out this distance but how can we  do that well let's focus just on these  three sides now let's rotate them so  it'll be a little easier to understand  the distance between the two endpoints  I'm going to join the three side with  the five side and then I'm going to  bring the four side to the left we have  a right triangle where one leg is four  and the other leg is three plus five  which equals eight we can solve for its  hypotenuse as the square root of the sum  of the squares of its sides this will be  the square root of 4 squared plus 8  squared so now let's go back to our  original diagram so we know this is the  same distance from endpoint to endpoint  and we're going to bring it back to our  unusual shape and now let's just focus  on this right triangle what is the value  of x in this right triangle well we know  that the length of the hypotenuse will  be the square root of 4 squared plus x  squared and it's also equal to the  square root of 4 squared plus 8 squared  therefore X is equal to 8 and that's our  answer I know there are other ways to  solve this problem but I thought this  one was very fun and I wanted to share  it with you thanks for watching and for  making mind your decisions one of the  best channels on YouTube  thanks for watching and thanks for your  support  [Music]
 

